✈️ Air Passengers Data Visualization using R

📌 Objective

The objective of this project is to analyze and visualize the Air Passengers dataset in R using a line chart to understand how the number of air passengers has increased over a given time period.
---

📁 Dataset Information

Dataset Name: Air Passengers

Data Type: Time series data

Time Period: 1949 to 1960

Frequency: Monthly

Description:
This dataset contains the monthly total number of international airline passengers. It helps in understanding long-term trends and seasonal patterns in air travel.

---

🛠️ Tools Used

R Programming Language

Built-in AirPassengers dataset in R

---

📊 Visualization Description

A line chart is used to represent the data.

The horizontal axis (X-axis) shows the time period (years).

The vertical axis (Y-axis) shows the number of air passengers.

Each point on the line represents passenger count for a particular month.

---

📈 Observations

The graph shows a clear increasing trend in the number of air passengers over time.

There are regular seasonal peaks, indicating higher passenger traffic during certain months every year.

After the mid-1950s, the growth in air passengers becomes faster, showing rapid expansion in air travel.

---

✅ Conclusion

The visualization clearly indicates that air passenger traffic has steadily increased from 1949 to 1960. This reflects:

Growth of the aviation industry

Increasing popularity of air travel

Presence of seasonal patterns in passenger movement

---

📌 Use Case

This project is useful for:

Time series analysis

Understanding trends and seasonality

Learning basic data visualization in R

Academic and beginner-level data science projects
